// Luo / Dholuo (luo) — Western Nilotic (Luo group), Latin orthography. Referee: en.wiktionary Luo (Wiktionary, HUMAN,
// 17 words — the ONLY source; no kaikki dump, no epitran luo-Latn, no wikipron). Single-source (🔷); consonants
// corroborated by Tucker (1994) 'A Grammar of Kenya Luo (Dholuo)'. The backbone (config.ts) already strips the
// referee's combining TONE + ATR diacritics (à̀ e̙ o̘) and the affricate tie bar; these folds neutralise the rest of
// what the orthography does NOT determine: the PRECOMPOSED tone-marked citation vowels (à ó ê í), syllable dots, the
// ±ATR vowel QUALITY (ɪ~i ɛ~e ɔ~o ʊ~u — unwritten harmony, we emit the +ATR default), the one-palatal notation
// (c ~ t͡ʃ ~ t͡ɕ), the palatalisation glide (ʲ~j), released-final aspiration (ʰ), the low-vowel fronting (æ~a), and the
// tap notation (r~ɾ).
